In the magic square shown, the sums of the numbers in each row, column, and diagonal are the same. Five of these numbers are represented by $a$, $b$, $c$, $d$, and $e$. Find $d+e$.

[asy]
path a=(0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle;
for (int i=0; i<3; ++i) {
for (int j=0; j<3; ++j) {
draw(shift((i,j))*a);
};}
label("30",(0.5,0.3),N);
label("$e$",(1.5,0.3),N);
label("18",(2.5,0.3),N);
label("15",(0.5,1.3),N);
label("$c$",(1.5,1.3),N);
label("$d$",(2.5,1.3),N);
